// [stmt.expr]: a delete-expression statement owns its `;` like any other
// expression statement. madc's delete statement recorded no terminator, so
// `delete p }` compiled and ran (exit 0).
// Oracle: g++ "error: expected ';' before '}' token", clang++ "error:
// expected ';' after expression".
int main() { int *p = new int; delete p }
